<h2 class="rule" id="update-check">Update an Existing Check</h2>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>POST SITE_ROOT/api/v3/checks/&lt;uuid&gt;
</code></pre></div>

<p>Updates an existing check and returns it. All request parameters are optional. If you
omit any parameter, SITE_NAME will leave its value unchanged. The check's status, its
pings and its flips do not change.</p>
<p>A <code>timeout</code> makes the check a Simple check, and a <code>schedule</code> makes it a Cron or
OnCalendar check, whatever kind it was before; with both, <code>schedule</code> wins.</p>
<p><strong>Authentication:</strong> a read-write key, in the <code>X-Api-Key</code> header or as an <code>api_key</code>
field of the body.</p>
<h3>Parameters</h3>
<p>The body fields are those of <a href="#create-check">Create a Check</a>, with the same types and
rules, and the <a href="#field-notes">field notes</a> apply; only the defaults differ.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Name</th>
<th>In</th>
<th>Type and allowed values</th>
<th>Required</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>uuid</code></td>
<td>path</td>
<td>UUID, lowercase with dashes</td>
<td>yes</td>
<td></td>
<td>The check to update.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>name</code>, <code>slug</code>, <code>tags</code>, <code>desc</code></td>
<td>body</td>
<td>strings, as for create</td>
<td>no</td>
<td>unchanged</td>
