<h2 class="rule" id="resume-check">Resume Monitoring of a Check</h2>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>POST SITE_ROOT/api/v3/checks/&lt;uuid&gt;/resume
</code></pre></div>

<p>Resumes a paused check. The check goes into the "new" state, and its last ping time
and any open run are cleared: like a newly created check, it waits for its first ping
and does not go down before it. Use this API call to resume the monitoring of checks
that are in the paused state, and have the <code>manual_resume</code> configuration parameter
set to <code>true</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Authentication:</strong> a read-write key, in the <code>X-Api-Key</code> header or as an <code>api_key</code>
field of a JSON body.</p>
<h3>Parameters</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Name</th>
<th>In</th>
<th>Type and allowed values</th>
<th>Required</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>uuid</code></td>
<td>path</td>
<td>UUID, lowercase with dashes</td>
<td>yes</td>
<td></td>
<td>The check to resume.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>The body may be empty.</p>
<h3>Example</h3>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>curl<span class="w"> </span>SITE_ROOT/api/v3/checks/7918b17b-a745-4db1-8575-9d2e07c97f79/resume<span class="w"> </span><span class="se">\</span>
<span class="w">    </span>--request<span class="w"> </span>POST<span class="w"> </span>--header<span class="w"> </span><span class="s2">"X-Api-Key: your-api-key"</span><span class="w"> </span>--data<span class="w"> </span><span class="s2">""</span>
</code></pre></div>

<p>Note: the <code>--data ""</code> argument forces curl to send a <code>Content-Length</code> request header
even though the request body is empty. For HTTP POST requests, the <code>Content-Length</code>
header is sometimes required by some network proxies and web servers.</p>
